  "provider_query": "Find the public X status from OpenAI that announces GPT-4",
  "answer": "The official OpenAI account post announcing GPT-4 is:\n\n**https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185**  \nPosted 2023-03-14 ~17:00 UTC by @OpenAI: “Announcing GPT-4, a large multimodal model, with our best-ever results on capabilities and alignment: https://openai.com/product/gpt-4” (video attached). [[1]](https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185)\n\nRelated public posts from the same launch window (concise sourcing):\n\n1. **@gdb** (Greg Brockman), 2023-03-14 17:00 UTC — “We’re releasing GPT-4…” with research link. https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426 [[2]](https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426)\n2. **@npew** (Peter Welinder, OpenAI), 2023-03-14 17:01 UTC — “GPT-4 is here…” ChatGPT / API waitlist. https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024 [[3]](https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024)\n3. **@sama** (Sam Altman), 2023-03-14 17:02 UTC — “here is GPT-4, our most capable and aligned model yet…” (thread). https://x.com/sama/status/1635687859494715393 [[4]](https://x.com/sama/status/1635687859494715393)\n4. **@miramurati** (then OpenAI CTO), 2023-03-14 17:03 UTC — “Unveiling GPT-4…” https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121 [[5]](https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121)\n5. **@verge**, 2023-03-14 17:06 UTC — coverage of the OpenAI announcement. https://x.com/verge/status/1635688829792268307 [[6]](https://x.com/verge/status/1635688829792268307)\n6. Coverage of the March 14, 2023 launch and later retirement context: The Verge write-up of the announcement. https://www.theverge.com/2023/3/14/23638033/openai-gpt-4-chatgpt-multimodal-deep-learning [[7]](https://www.theverge.com/2023/3/14/23638033/openai-gpt-4-chatgpt-multimodal-deep-learning)\n7. Later note (not the announcement): Ars Technica on GPT-4’s March 2023 debut and 2025 ChatGPT retirement. https://arstechnica.com/ai/2025/04/the-ai-that-sparked-tech-panic-and-scared-world-leaders-heads-to-retirement/ [[8]](https://arstechnica.com/ai/2025/04/the-ai-that-sparked-tech-panic-and-scared-world-leaders-heads-to-retirement/)",
